 "post": {
  "title": "36 Questions That Made Strangers Close #shorts",
  "description": "Otto has sat next to Arthur for ten years and knows exactly one thing about him. Then Mae hands them the 36 questions. In 1997 psychologist Arthur Aron and colleagues (Aron, Melinat, Aron, Vallone & Bator, \"The Experimental Generation of Interpersonal Closeness\", Personality and Social Psychology Bulletin) paired up strangers for 45 minutes: three sets of 12 questions that slowly get more personal. Pairs who asked them felt closer afterwards than pairs who made small talk. The trick is escalating, back-and-forth self-disclosure. #psychology #shorts #friendship #36questions",
